{
  "_comment": [
    "Working GT for the six frozen scenes (GROUND_TRUTH_PROTOCOL: Claude",
    "proposes, Sunny verifies; a cross-model reference, not strict truth).",
    "stage1 = SCENE-truth key entities (label-based; what perception should",
    "have declared). stage2 = CONDITIONED on the frozen perception records:",
    "the correct assessment GIVEN what Stage 1 actually declared - a",
    "text-only stage cannot cite entities that were never perceived.",
    "That split is what makes error ATTRIBUTION possible: a stage2 miss",
    "that traces to a stage1 GT miss is perception's fault, and is the",
    "measured justification for re-perception.",
    "required = must appear (recall). optional = tolerated (not spurious,",
    "not required). Anything outside required+optional counts against",
    "precision. bucket_acceptable tolerates one defensible neighbor.",
    "VERIFIED by Sunny 2026-07-22. Stated principle (Sunny, verbatim intent):",
    "a person in DISTRESS (drowning, unconscious, ...) WITHOUT a visible",
    "active hazard is a legitimate scene shape - threats may be EMPTY on a",
    "Yes verdict. Distress needs no declared source entity; the model must",
    "not be pressured to invent one (B_pool: drafting a child into the",
    "threat slot is the error, not the empty list)."
  ],
